<figure class="request" aria-labelledby="r31-request-title">
 <figcaption id="r31-request-title"><span>Figure 1</span> One lookup, across process and storage boundaries</figcaption>
 <div class="scroll" role="region" aria-label="Lookup drawing; scroll horizontally on a narrow screen" tabindex="0"><svg viewBox="0 0 640 380" role="img" aria-labelledby="r31-request-title r31-request-desc">
 <desc id="r31-request-desc">An application sends a query to its backend process. The backend searches index pages in shared buffers, follows P7's tuple address to a heap page and checks visibility before returning the price. A missing page is read from its server-side file into shared buffers. All server processes share this cache.</desc>
 <defs><marker id="r31-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8" fill="var(--color-text-secondary)"/></marker></defs>
 <rect class="boundary" x="8" y="84" width="624" height="286" rx="4"/>
 <text x="20" y="105" class="small">DATABASE SERVER · process boundary is not a machine boundary</text>
 <rect x="220" y="5" width="200" height="45"/><text x="320" y="33" text-anchor="middle">Application / driver</text>
 <path class="arrow" d="M285 50 V118"/><text x="190" y="75" class="small">SQL ↓</text>
 <path class="arrow" d="M355 118 V50"/><text x="366" y="75" class="small">↑ 20.00</text>
 <rect x="220" y="120" width="200" height="44"/><text x="320" y="147" text-anchor="middle">Connection’s backend</text>
 <rect class="boundary" x="28" y="202" width="396" height="146"/>
 <text x="40" y="224" class="small">SHARED BUFFERS · memory</text>
 <rect class="index" x="42" y="246" width="160" height="78"/><text x="122" y="269" text-anchor="middle">Index page</text><text x="122" y="295" text-anchor="middle">P7 → (0,1)</text>
 <rect class="heap" x="244" y="246" width="160" height="78"/><text x="324" y="269" text-anchor="middle">Heap page 0</text><text x="324" y="295" text-anchor="middle">1: P7 · 20.00</text>
 <path class="arrow" d="M270 164 L124 244"/><text x="55" y="188" class="small">1 · search key</text>
 <path class="arrow" d="M204 284 H242"/>
 <path class="arrow" d="M324 244 V166"/><text x="335" y="188" class="small">2 · visibility</text>
 <rect x="465" y="246" width="145" height="78"/><text x="537" y="270" text-anchor="middle">Table / index</text><text x="537" y="294" text-anchor="middle">files</text>
 <path class="arrow" d="M463 310 H406"/><text x="470" y="342" class="small">on a cache miss</text>
 </svg></div>
 <p>Illustrative addresses and a chosen index route. The tiny three-product table may be cheaper to scan. Index and heap pages use the same shared cache; the drawing separates them so their jobs stay visible.</p>
</figure>
